From 80b6908b049069749bd72cdc37d9e5c47e2da050 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 19:48:14 +0600
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] Unify ethics layer: extract Learning Core, add store.py,
 integrate ethics/aethel_council/threads

Splits the A1/A2/A3 evidence/heat math out of ethical_core.py into a new
heat.py module (the Learning Core) so there is one implementation of the
hyperbolic open-interval law, not a duplicate per consumer.
ethical_core.py's compute_evidence()/compute_heat() now delegate to it;
all existing callers (unified_core.py, etc.) are unaffected.

Adds store.py, a real entity-persistence layer on the same context2.db
schema storage.py already defines. Trust-pattern heat is always
re-derived from the full event history rather than cached as a drifting
mutable scalar, matching the existing scar-heat discipline in ethics.py.

Integrates three modules from a parallel session's work that depended on
heat.py/store.py existing: ethics.py (observe-only valence/conflict/
trust/provenance layer), aethel_council.py (level-platform disagreement
resolution registry), and threads.py (commit-trailer routing over the
same evidence machinery).

Adds 25 tests (test_heat.py, test_store.py, test_ethics.py) covering the
new modules and the ethical_core.py delegation. Full suite: 145/145
passing, no regressions.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
